From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: fix WiFi.Reset() for complete factory reset including
 user-created VAPs

This patch implements complete factory reset: all APs (including
user-created guest VAPs), EndPoints, and parameter values are restored
to factory defaults when WiFi.Reset() is called.

--- Feature: delete user-created VAPs before radio stop ---

User-created VAPs (added via addVAPIntf after startup) must be removed
during factory reset. They persist in the DM with Enable=false after
the existing reset logic, which is not a complete factory reset.

Implementation: record T_Radio.nrDefaultAps at the end of
wld_persist_onStart() after the defaults ODL is first loaded. This
gives the baseline AP count per radio. During _Reset(), iterate each
radio and delete any APs beyond this baseline count.

Critically, this deletion happens BEFORE wld_rad_doRadioReset(). While
the radio is still up, s_deinitAP() can call mfn_wrad_delvapif() to
properly tear down the kernel VAP interface. After radio stop, the
kernel interfaces are already gone and delvapif would be a no-op,
leaving stale DM/C-struct state.

Each extra AP is deleted together with its linked SSID instance (same
pattern as _delVAPIntf).

--- Bug 1: ODL re-parse aborts for ALL objects in the tree ---

amxd_object_add_action_cb() and amxd_param_add_action_cb() both return
amxd_status_unknown_error when the same (fn, priv=NULL) pair is already
registered. Both object->cb_fns and param->cb_fns are drained directly
via amxc_llist_for_each since both remove_action_cb APIs have
when_null(fn, exit) guards making them no-ops for fn=NULL.

--- Bug 2: EP-linked SSIDs remain enabled after reset ---

pEP->enable = 0 does not update the DM Enable parameter. Fix: write
Enable=false via transaction for each EndPoint and its linked SSID.

--- Bug 3: EndPoint "Fail to create instance" after reset ---

The defaults ODL fires _wld_ep_addInstance_oaf which only supports
fresh creation. Fix: delete all EndPoint instances before ODL reload.
EP-linked SSIDs are preserved (not re-created by static ODL parser).

--- Bug 4: signal drain loop hangs indefinitely ---

Fix: bound the drain loop to 1000 iterations.

--- Bug 5: factory reset not durable across reboot ---

Fix: add wld_persist_deleteSavedConf() and call it from _Reset().

Signed-off-by: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 include/wld/Features/wld_persist.h     |  1 +
 include/wld/wld.h                      |  1 +
 src/Features/persist/wld_persist_off.c | 14 +++++++++++
 src/Features/persist/wld_persist_on.c  | 26 +++++++++++++++++
 src/wld.c                              | 126 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 168 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/wld/Features/wld_persist.h b/include/wld/Features/wld_persist.h
